<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $23.95 bln on Dec 20.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $23.95 bln on Dec 20.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $23.95 billion on December 20, 1996 from $23.81 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Dec 20	Dec 13	 Dec 22</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,603	19,418	 17,302</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,347	 4,347	  4,429</p>
<p>    SDRs				    --	    42	    138</p>
<p>    Total			     23,950	23,807	 21,869</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
